NEbBDHaGbzHSFAX6ybVmjlFhd52D-xaJDTan6GNamOahZrD46YlInY5OifkimAaDl7PwcYoiYDV0Tba9nLD5Z3D9kpDOFsf5ZUgxbCaNbYH-LpxZw-SSvhWMaub_F5qm3LZGKo8tDgOvJT6NxD-G6nLtdshnhW2l1TU_KqOX1OehG6JjtCgMS1w2dloX7X49JkxTnu82IY-sWLzfiNPAK9D-cw8uLHoCFLMYp-wHc94RyFu4G7rPHP70v6qjK70aitC7Qb3mHpT9Yfy2tyRYK-ZrPiNBdcnr9p21gVOihpa66GF7wnf4efSW2YP8PfLnR1\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Exploring repository management**\\n\\nI’m considering whether to commit changes for the nested repository since the user wants a clean workspace. Committing those changes, along with updating the top-level git link, might help. However, I'm not sure if the user prefers this approach. \\n\\nI might also need to include new .gitignore files for both the nested and root repositories. Additionally, setting up cron jobs for alerts and possibly running it now could enhance the process. Lastly, I might have to adjust certain patterns in the .gitignore to avoid over-ignoring important files.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating untracked directories**\\n\\nI’m contemplating whether to track the `skills/` and `projects/` directories since there are many uncommitted changes affecting progress. It seems worth committing the `skills/` directories, as those might be important. Since the user mentioned significant uncommitted changes, I think it’s best to commit meaningful content and ignore unnecessary files.\\n\\nI could just stage and commit the workspace governance along with the .gitignore while leaving the existing untracked project assets for now. But that still feels incomplete. I might just create ignores for obvious generated files and keep the essential directories visible to commit tracked changes effectively.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Configuring cron jobs**\\n\\nI’m thinking about adjusting the cron job to run at 07:55, since the user expects it earlier, but it’s currently set for 08:00. There might be a delay on certain days due to failures, so adding a failure alert for the current user on Feishu could be helpful. Also, I should ensure there’s no stagger and possibly extend the timeout. \\n\\nI noticed the cron job only uses one model, so if the model fails, there won't be a fallback. Therefore, I should add alerts after just one error and configure that properly.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"我准备这样落地，不绕弯：\n\n- **workspace 整理**：  \n  把明显的运行产物/生成图片/本地状态从 git 视野里剥掉，只留下真正要维护的内容；顺手把当前这批有效改动做一次提交，避免继续越堆越乱。\n\n- **日报 cron 修正**：  \n  保留 OpenClaw 内建 cron 作为唯一方案；把“外部 shell 脚本”降级为备用；给 `morning-briefing` 补上失败告警和更稳的执行参数，避免再次“到了点没报，事后才发现”。\n\n我直接改。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_090b64d726cd28200169c3387fd88c81919bb0cb05c83115a6\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AmdhLi5StmihOIDeSflDQHCI|fc_090b64d726cd28200169c3388009ac8191a98ac38ff0bdbe62","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/.gitignore","content":"# Local runtime state\n.openclaw/\n.clawhub/\nlogs/\nskills/.skills_store_lock.json\n\n# OS / editor\n.DS_Store\n*.swp\n*.swo\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n\n# Secrets\n.env\n.env.*\n\n# Local trash\n.trash/\n\n# Local scratch / learning state\n.learnings/\n.tasks/\n\n# Generated image outputs\napple_seedream*.png\nskills-5p-*.png\ntest*.png\nxhs_*.jpg\nxhs_cover*.jpg\nxiaohongshu-cover-*.png\nxiaohongshu-cover-v*.png\nxiaohongshu-canghe-*.png\nxiaohongshu-canghe-top3*.png\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/.gitignore\",\"content\":\"# Local runtime state\\n.openclaw/\\n.clawhub/\\nlogs/\\nskills/.skills_store_lock.json\\n\\n# OS / editor\\n.DS_Store\\n*.swp\\n*.swo\\n__pycache__/\\n*.pyc\\n\\n# Secrets\\n.env\\n.env.*\\n\\n# Local trash\\n.trash/\\n\\n# Local scratch / learning state\\n.learnings/\\n.tasks/\\n\\n# Generated image outputs\\napple_seedream*.png\\nskills-5p-*.png\\ntest*.png\\nxhs_*.jpg\\nxhs_cover*.jpg\\nxiaohongshu-cover-*.png\\nxiaohongshu-cover-v*.png\\nxiaohongshu-canghe-*.png\\nxiaohongshu-canghe-top3*.png\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex